&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/y12ne-bogan-weekly-news#bpx42aowpj"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bpx42aowpj-bh8qc4w12s-bto8crem3z-b9x4odiux2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>School Health Guidelines: When to Stay Home</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/y12ne-bogan-weekly-news#bfk3x3z2v4</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Students should &lt;strong&gt;stay home&lt;/strong&gt; if they have: fever of 100°F or higher, vomiting or diarrhea within 24 hours, undiagnosed rash with fever, active head lice, sore throat with fever/swollen glands/strep, eye infection with discharge, severe respiratory illness, or feel too sick to participate. Students can &lt;strong&gt;return when&lt;/strong&gt;: fever-free for 24 hours without medicine, vomiting resolved overnight and can hold down food, diarrhea improved to no more than 2 accidents per 24 hours, rash cleared by doctor, lice treatment completed, 12-24 hours after antibiotics (for strep/eye infection), or respiratory symptoms improving for 24 hours and fever-free. &lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy&lt;/strong&gt; by washing hands, covering coughs, and being kind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/y12ne-bogan-weekly-news#bfk3x3z2v4"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bfk3x3z2v4-b27mhl6bz5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>September is Attendance Awareness Month</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/y12ne-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;September is Attendance Awareness Month&lt;/strong&gt; at Talawanda High School. Ohio defines chronic absenteeism as missing 10% or more of the year (both excused and unexcused absences), and this includes hours missed from tardies and early dismissals, not just full days. Families will receive monthly letters if their child reaches 10% or more absences, and the school encourages families to reach out if they need assistance with attendance issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/y12ne-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bjqvo7kz71-bfmqdkhp7i</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Unplug and Play Playground Event</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unplug and Play&lt;/strong&gt; event at the Bogan playground on &lt;strong&gt;Thursday, September 10&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;strong&gt;5:30pm-7:30pm&lt;/strong&gt;. Students can hang out with friends, see their teachers, and enjoy popsicles. The event features playground equipment including a yellow slide, and sports activities with soccer and football available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add to Calendar:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&amp;text=Unplug%20and%20Play%20at%20Bogan%20Playground&amp;dates=20260910T173000/20260910T193000&amp;details=%2A%2AUnplug%20and%20Play%2A%2A%20event%20at%20the%20Bogan%20playground%20on%20%2A%2AThursday%2C%20September%2010%2A%2A%20from%20%2A%2A5%3A30pm-7%3A30pm%2A%2A.%20Students%20can%20hang%20out%20with%20friends%2C%20see%20their%20teachers%2C%20and%20enjoy%20popsicles.%20The%20event%20features%20&amp;location=Bogan%20playground"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="data:text/calendar;charset=utf-8,BEGIN%3AVCALENDAR%0AVERSION%3A2.0%0ABEGIN%3AVEVENT%0ADTSTART%3A20260910T173000%0ADTEND%3A20260910T193000%0ASUMMARY%3AUnplug%20and%20Play%20at%20Bogan%20Playground%0ADESCRIPTION%3A%2A%2AUnplug%20and%20Play%2A%2A%20event%20at%20the%20Bogan%20playground%20on%20%2A%2AThursday%2C%20September%2010%2A%2A%20from%20%2A%2A5%3A30pm-7%3A30pm%2A%2A.%20Students%20can%20hang%20out%20with%20friends%2C%20see%20their%20teachers%2C%20and%20enjoy%20popsicles.%20The%20event%20features%20%0ALOCATION%3ABogan%20playground%0AEND%3AVEVENT%0AEND%3AVCALENDAR"&gt;iCal&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose?subject=Unplug%20and%20Play%20at%20Bogan%20Playground&amp;startdt=20260910T173000&amp;enddt=20260910T193000&amp;body=%2A%2AUnplug%20and%20Play%2A%2A%20event%20at%20the%20Bogan%20playground%20on%20%2A%2AThursday%2C%20September%2010%2A%2A%20from%20%2A%2A5%3A30pm-7%3A30pm%2A%2A.%20Students%20can%20hang%20out%20with%20friends%2C%20see%20their%20teachers%2C%20and%20enjoy%20popsicles.%20The%20event%20features%20&amp;location=Bogan%20playground"&gt;Outlook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bjqvo7kz71-b74m6trbab</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>September 2026 Breakfast Menu Available</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bfr77vevhd</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;September 2026 breakfast menu&lt;/strong&gt; for Bogan Elementary is now available. The menu includes a rotating selection of items throughout the month such as Mini Chocolate Chip French Toast, Stuffed Hash Brown, Glazed Donuts, Sausage &amp;amp; Cheese Biscuit Sandwiches, Mini Pancake Sausage Wraps, Cinnamon Buns, Egg &amp;amp; Cheese options, Apple Cinnamon Swirl Texas Toast, Biscuits &amp;amp; Sausage Gravy, Mini Powdered Donuts, Cinnamon French Toast Sticks, Breakfast Pizza, and Glazed Donut Pull-Apart. &lt;strong&gt;100% fruit juice, fresh fruit, and milk are included with every breakfast.&lt;/strong&gt; No school on September 8th and 18th (Labor Day on September 7th).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bfr77vevhd"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bfr77vevhd-byjfy5ixy6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>PAX Good Behavior Game Calendar</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#berhllupn2</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAX (Peace, Productivity, Health, Happiness)&lt;/strong&gt; is a research-based classroom strategy that helps students make positive choices and collaborate with others. The program promotes kindness, teamwork, and respectful behavior to create a calmer, more focused learning environment. A &lt;strong&gt;September 2026 Student Calendar&lt;/strong&gt; provides daily PAX activities including: celebrating Classical Music Month, drawing homework visions, making cards for friends/family, holding doors open, creating Group Granny projects, exercising with friends, and participating in National Read-a-Book Day (Sept 6) and National Positive Thinking Day (Sept 13).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;National Read-a-Book Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add to Calendar:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&amp;text=National%20Read-a-Book%20Day&amp;dates=20260906/20260907&amp;details=%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="data:text/calendar;charset=utf-8,BEGIN%3AVCALENDAR%0AVERSION%3A2.0%0ABEGIN%3AVEVENT%0ADTSTART%3A20260906%0ADTEND%3A20260907%0ASUMMARY%3ANational%20Read-a-Book%20Day%0ADESCRIPTION%3A%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20%0ALOCATION%3ATalawanda%20High%20School%0AEND%3AVEVENT%0AEND%3AVCALENDAR"&gt;iCal&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose?subject=National%20Read-a-Book%20Day&amp;startdt=20260906&amp;enddt=20260907&amp;body=%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Outlook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;National Positive Thinking Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add to Calendar:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&amp;text=National%20Positive%20Thinking%20Day&amp;dates=20260913/20260914&amp;details=%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="data:text/calendar;charset=utf-8,BEGIN%3AVCALENDAR%0AVERSION%3A2.0%0ABEGIN%3AVEVENT%0ADTSTART%3A20260913%0ADTEND%3A20260914%0ASUMMARY%3ANational%20Positive%20Thinking%20Day%0ADESCRIPTION%3A%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20%0ALOCATION%3ATalawanda%20High%20School%0AEND%3AVEVENT%0AEND%3AVCALENDAR"&gt;iCal&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose?subject=National%20Positive%20Thinking%20Day&amp;startdt=20260913&amp;enddt=20260914&amp;body=%2A%2APAX%20%28Peace%2C%20Productivity%2C%20Health%2C%20Happiness%29%2A%2A%20is%20a%20research-based%20classroom%20strategy%20that%20helps%20students%20make%20positive%20choices%20and%20collaborate%20with%20others.%20The%20program%20promotes%20kindness%2C%20teamwork%2C%20&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Outlook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#berhllupn2"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">berhllupn2-bbyw57cizv-bbwiju01hj</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>School Social Worker Introduction and Services</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Emily is the School Social Worker for the 2026-2027 school year. She provides &lt;strong&gt;student support&lt;/strong&gt; for mental health needs and additional support options, &lt;strong&gt;resource guidance&lt;/strong&gt; including food/hygiene support, clothing, rent/utilities assistance, and holiday assistance, and &lt;strong&gt;food support&lt;/strong&gt; through a Little FREE Pantry outside Bogan, weekly Power Packs, family food boxes, and donations. Contact her at whitee@talawanda.org or 513-273-3403.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bcwm1-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bh1mh3rers-b1j5poder9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>PAX Good Behavior Game Program</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#berhllupn2</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;PAX Good Behavior Game&lt;/strong&gt; is a research-based classroom strategy that promotes positive student choices and collaboration. The program supports a calmer, more focused learning environment by encouraging kindness, teamwork, and respectful behavior among students.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students have access to monthly calendars with daily PAX activities including acts of kindness, skill-building exercises, and family engagement opportunities throughout August and September 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#berhllupn2"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">berhllupn2-bbyw57cizv-bb8yodd1n6-bbwiju01hj</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Social Work Spotlight</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers</link><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a spotlight feature on the social work services available at Talawanda High School. The item appears to be a header or announcement introducing information about the school's social work department and resources available to students.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bh1mh3rers</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>School Bus Safety Code of Conduct</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bhgawjxij4</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Talawanda prioritizes bus safety with a progressive discipline system for misconduct. Violations result in escalating consequences: 1st offense - warning and conference; 2nd - parent call and documentation; 3rd - 3-day suspension; 4th - 5-day bus suspension with parent conference; 5th - removal from bus for semester or minimum 10 days. &lt;strong&gt;Key safety rules&lt;/strong&gt;: stay seated facing forward, keep aisle clear, listen to driver, don't distract driver, wait for driver's signal before crossing, and always cross in front of bus while looking both ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bhgawjxij4"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bhgawjxij4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>McCullough-Hyde Foundation Grant for Family Events</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Bogan Elementary received a &lt;strong&gt;$3,000 grant&lt;/strong&gt; from the McCullough-Hyde Foundation to host family and student engagement events. Social worker Emily White wrote the grant, which will fund three events: a &lt;strong&gt;Books &amp;amp; Breakfast in fall&lt;/strong&gt;, a &lt;strong&gt;STEM &amp;amp; Math Night in spring&lt;/strong&gt;, and an &lt;strong&gt;Unplug &amp;amp; Play event&lt;/strong&gt; at year's end. The photo shows staff receiving a ceremonial check dated June 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bjqvo7kz71-bq8x2b6ej3-b1l5wiubvl</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>PTG Fall Programs: Mumkins and Reading at Home</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bpx42aowpj</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mumkins and Mumsters&lt;/strong&gt; are back! Sales run September 2-16 with delivery on October 3rd. These decorative items are made from recycled, eco-friendly, and reusable materials.&lt;/p&gt;
