&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reading at Home (RAH) Program Starts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add to Calendar:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&amp;text=Reading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%20Program%20Starts&amp;dates=20260911/20260912&amp;details=%2A%2AMumkins%20and%20Mumsters%2A%2A%20are%20back%21%20Sales%20run%20September%202-16%20with%20delivery%20on%20October%203rd.%20These%20decorative%20items%20are%20made%20from%20recycled%2C%20eco-friendly%2C%20and%20reusable%20materials.%0A%0A%2A%2AReading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%2A&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="data:text/calendar;charset=utf-8,BEGIN%3AVCALENDAR%0AVERSION%3A2.0%0ABEGIN%3AVEVENT%0ADTSTART%3A20260911%0ADTEND%3A20260912%0ASUMMARY%3AReading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%20Program%20Starts%0ADESCRIPTION%3A%2A%2AMumkins%20and%20Mumsters%2A%2A%20are%20back%21%20Sales%20run%20September%202-16%20with%20delivery%20on%20October%203rd.%20These%20decorative%20items%20are%20made%20from%20recycled%2C%20eco-friendly%2C%20and%20reusable%20materials.%0A%0A%2A%2AReading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%2A%0ALOCATION%3ATalawanda%20High%20School%0AEND%3AVEVENT%0AEND%3AVCALENDAR"&gt;iCal&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose?subject=Reading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%20Program%20Starts&amp;startdt=20260911&amp;enddt=20260912&amp;body=%2A%2AMumkins%20and%20Mumsters%2A%2A%20are%20back%21%20Sales%20run%20September%202-16%20with%20delivery%20on%20October%203rd.%20These%20decorative%20items%20are%20made%20from%20recycled%2C%20eco-friendly%2C%20and%20reusable%20materials.%0A%0A%2A%2AReading%20at%20Home%20%28RAH%29%2A&amp;location=Talawanda%20High%20School"&gt;Outlook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/cqjvne-bogan-weekly-news#bpx42aowpj"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bpx42aowpj-bh8qc4w12s-bamkc9zs79</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Meet Mrs. Emily - School Social Worker</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Emily is Talawanda High School's social worker for the 2026-2027 school year. She provides &lt;strong&gt;student support&lt;/strong&gt; for mental health needs and additional support, &lt;strong&gt;resource guidance&lt;/strong&gt; including food/hygiene support, clothing, shoes, coats, rent/utilities assistance, and holiday assistance, and &lt;strong&gt;food support&lt;/strong&gt; through a Little FREE Pantry outside Bogan, weekly Power Packs, family food boxes, and donations. Contact her at &lt;strong&gt;whitee@talawanda.org&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;513-273-3403&lt;/strong&gt; for any needs or questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bh1mh3rers"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bh1mh3rers-bu9e2anrtp</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>PBIS Cafeteria Expectations Program</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bd03u7m4qz</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Talawanda High School continues its &lt;strong&gt;Positive Behavioral Interventions and Supports (PBIS)&lt;/strong&gt; program with exciting student recognition opportunities. Students can earn &lt;strong&gt;Bogan Brave Tickets&lt;/strong&gt; from staff for following expectations, with weekly Friday prize drawings by Dr. Cannon. Monthly &lt;strong&gt;Student of the Month&lt;/strong&gt; awards recognize students demonstrating specific character traits, earning certificates, photos, and Good News Calls home. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cafeteria expectations&lt;/strong&gt; include: &lt;strong&gt;Be Kind&lt;/strong&gt; (use appropriate language, say please/thank you, welcome everyone, help peers, listen to tablemates), &lt;strong&gt;Be Safe&lt;/strong&gt; (enter/exit quietly with walking feet, stay seated, keep hands/feet to self, share food only from share table), and &lt;strong&gt;Be Responsible&lt;/strong&gt; (use 3-inch voice, raise hand for help, follow adult directions, use tools appropriately, keep table and floor clean).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bd03u7m4qz"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bd03u7m4qz-b445rh3fvc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>New Staff and Position Changes at Bogan</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Bogan welcomes several new staff members for the 2026-27 school year, including teachers &lt;strong&gt;Kiersten Weaver&lt;/strong&gt; (preschool), &lt;strong&gt;Jessica Whitaker&lt;/strong&gt; (kindergarten), &lt;strong&gt;Ainsley Stone&lt;/strong&gt; (SLP), and &lt;strong&gt;Kate Banger&lt;/strong&gt; (OT), as well as paraprofessionals, therapist, custodian, and lunch monitor. Additionally, three current staff members have moved to new positions: &lt;strong&gt;Skylar Pittman&lt;/strong&gt; (2nd grade), &lt;strong&gt;Allison James&lt;/strong&gt; (4th grade ELA/Social Studies), and &lt;strong&gt;Betty Williams&lt;/strong&gt; (4th &amp;amp; 5th Grade Title Reading).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bjqvo7kz71"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bjqvo7kz71-bv0z34o44e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Around Talawanda Newsletter Header</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bwk8x8y5ub</link><description>&lt;p&gt;This appears to be a header or title page for the "Around Talawanda" newsletter section. No specific content, events, or announcements are included in this item beyond the section heading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bwk8x8y5ub"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bwk8x8y5ub-b5j73qfe5d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>August Cafeteria Menus and Lunch Accounts</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#b0srpil80f</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lunch account reminders:&lt;/strong&gt; Parents can add funds to student lunch accounts through PaySchool Central and should keep accounts current. Contact Mrs. White for assistance with lunch debt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;August 2026 menus available:&lt;/strong&gt; Breakfast options include items like Breakfast Pizza, Egg &amp;amp; Cheese Biscuit Sandwich, Mini Powdered Donuts, and Sausage &amp;amp; Cheese Biscuit Sandwich. Lunch options include Crispy Popcorn Chicken, 4x6 Rectangle Cheese Pizza, Cheeseburger on a Bun, and Tony's Deep Dish Cheese Pizza. 100% fruit juice, oranges or other fresh fruit, and choice of milk are included with every meal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#b0srpil80f"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">b0srpil80f-b570fb3xuh-bfr77vevhd-b2e2a54rwt-bgn99km4oo</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>School Nurse Welcome and Health Requirements</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bfk3x3z2v4</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The school nurse welcomes families back and reminds &lt;strong&gt;Kindergarten families&lt;/strong&gt; to submit required &lt;strong&gt;physical and immunization records&lt;/strong&gt;. Students needing medication during school must complete a &lt;strong&gt;School Medication Permit&lt;/strong&gt; form (available at https://www.talawanda.org/media/user/resources/Form_SchoolMedicalPermit.pdf), which must be filled out by a healthcare provider for prescribed medications. For questions or concerns, contact the nurse at &lt;strong&gt;Bears@talawanda.org&lt;/strong&gt; (preferred) or by phone, though response times may vary as student care is the top priority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bfk3x3z2v4"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bfk3x3z2v4-bxfvdhiddj</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Student Attendance Policy and Chronic Absenteeism</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bfmqdkhp7i</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attendance is essential for student success.&lt;/strong&gt; Ohio defines chronic absenteeism as missing 10% or more of the school year (excused or unexcused), calculated by hours missed—including tardies and early dismissals. Families will receive monthly letters if their student reaches 10% absence threshold. The school encourages families to take planned trips but asks them to be mindful of other absences, and offers help for any attendance concerns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/9xcjr-bogan-weekly-news#bfmqdkhp7i"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bfmqdkhp7i</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item></channel></rss>